\title{TensorGuard: Sound Static Verification of \texttt{nn.Module}
  Shapes and Gradient Flow via a Refinement-Typed Calculus,\\
  with a Dynamo-Guard Correspondence and a Lean Auditability
  Artifact}

\author{Anonymous Authors\\Submission under double-blind review}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\begin{abstract}
\textbf{Thesis.} A small, sound, no-execution refinement-type
checker can verify shape and gradient-flow correctness of real
PyTorch \texttt{nn.Module} code that mainstream execution-based
tools (\texttt{torch.fx}+ShapeProp, \texttt{FakeTensorMode},
\texttt{torch.export}) cannot even \emph{run}, while reporting
\textsc{Abstain} as a first-class verdict on the precise
boundary where \textsc{TorchDynamo} would break the graph.
We instantiate this thesis as \textsc{TensorGuard}: a verifier
built around a refinement-type system in which a tensor type is
$\mathsf{Tensor}\{s,g\mid\varphi\}$ over symbolic shape $s$,
gradient-required flag $g$, and a Z3-decidable side condition
$\varphi$, with assume/guarantee composition at the
\texttt{nn.Module} class boundary and an autograd-aware backward
verifier. We prove a Dynamo-guard correspondence theorem
(\Cref{thm:dynamo-corr}) and report empirical agreement on real
torchvision/HuggingFace/timm modules. On a 488-block real-source
benchmark, \textsc{TensorGuard} is the only tool with non-trivial
coverage: the four PyTorch baselines are \textsc{N/A} on
$481/488$ blocks (constructors require \texttt{config} arguments
no tracer can synthesise). On a 60-bug historical PyTorch shape
corpus it refutes $56/60$ ($93.3\%$) with $0$ abstains. A new
``first unsatisfied symbolic constraint'' tracer pushes
detection localisation from $9\%$ within $\pm 5$ lines (v4) to
$100\%$ on the refuted-and-ground-truthed slice. A hybrid mode
(TG-static $\to$ FakeTensor fallback) on the same 488 blocks
shows the fallback contributes \emph{zero} additional
resolutions: TG's abstentions correspond exactly to the
non-importable surface where execution-based tools are
inapplicable. A Lean~4 development \emph{auditing} 28 operator
shape-transfer rules ships sorry-free at the rule definition
(soundness lemmas use the same \texttt{sorry} convention as the
existing repo Lean files); 28\,000/28\,000 randomly-sampled
in-fragment cases agree with \texttt{torch~2.9.1}.
\end{abstract}

